 <iati-activity default-currency="EUR" hierarchy="2" humanitarian="0" iati-activities:version="2.02" xml:lang="EN" xmlns:iati-activities="http://d-portal.org/xmlns/iati-activities" xmlns:xsd="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema" xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance">
  <iati-identifier>NL-KVK-40409352-PRJ13-196-0002</iati-identifier>
  <reporting-org ref="NL-KVK-40409352" type="21">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Netherlands Red Cross</narrative>
  </reporting-org>
  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">NLRC-MoFA Partnership: Evaluations &amp; Thematic Studies</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Learning as part of the NLRC-MoFA 2022-2026 partnership. The &apos;project&apos; consists of:
- a partnership midterm review;
- a partnership final evaluation;
- a number of thematic studies.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The midterm review and final evaluation will be conducted by external consultants to ensure independency. For the thematic studies, the team will be more mixed, and may consist of RCRC actors, knowledge institutes, universities and consultants.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="3">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The primary audience for the learning products are the NLRC and MoFA. In addition, direct implementing partners within the RCRC Movement (NSs &amp; IFRC) are also main stakeholders. In particular the thematic studies, are expected to be disseminated to a wider audience, the humanitarian sector more broadly.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The project on the one hand ensures accountability; to the donor, affected populations and other stakeholders. On the other hand, it will facilitate learning for the current partnership and beyond, to improve humanitarian programming in the long run.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The reach of the partnership is global. However, there is expected to be more focus on the countries in which NLRC has a long-term partnership with the NS, these are: CAR, Ethiopia, Haiti, Ivory Coast, Lebanon, Mali, oPT, Philippines, South Sudan, Sudan, Uganda, and Zambia.</narrative>
  </description>
